    "process_step": "#########\n# GDSC ETL is performed in two steps: shell script to ETL data into postgres\n# and then additional transformations with SQL in postGIS (if needed).\n####\n\n#########\n# Step 1 - bash script (pseudo code)\n####\n\n# create directory structure and move into it\nmkdir -p /data/mdc_county_park_boundaries/download -p /data/mdc_county_park_boundaries/etl\nchmod -R 777 /data/mdc_county_park_boundaries\ncd /data/mdc_county_park_boundaries\n\n# set update flag based on last update and update frequency\ndo_update=0 if date() < last_update + update_frequency else do_update = 1\n\n# download if update flag is set:\nif do_update == 1 then\nwget --retry-connrefused --waitretry=1 --read-timeout=20 --timeout=15 -t 10 -O download/mdc_county_park_boundaries.geojson 'https://services.arcgis.com/8Pc9XBTAsYuxx9Ny/arcgis/rest/services/CountyParkBoundaries_PROS_View_for_ALWAYS_ON/FeatureServer/1/query?outFields=*&where=1%3D1&spatialRefId=4326&f=geojson' 2>&1\n\n# load into postGIS with:\nogr2ogr -lco GEOMETRY_NAME=geom -f PostgreSQL PG:\"<postgres connection>\" download/mdc_county_park_boundaries.geojson -nlt multipolygon -nln mdc_county_park_boundaries\necho success: mdc_county_park_boundaries.geojson loaded with ogr2ogr\n\n\n#########\n# Step 2 - SQL script (pseudo code):\n####\n\n# remove duplicate points and make geometries valid:\nUPDATE mdc_county_park_boundaries\n  SET geom=ST_MakeValid(ST_RemoveRepeatedPoints(geom));\n\n# add local geometry column and reproject existing geometries into local EPSG:\nALTER TABLE mdc_county_park_boundaries DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS geom_local CASCADE;\nSELECT AddGeometryColumn (\n  'mdc_county_park_boundaries',\n  'geom_local', 2236, 'multipolygon', 2\n);\nUPDATE mdc_county_park_boundaries\n  SET geom_local=ST_MakeValid(ST_RemoveRepeatedPoints(ST_Transform(ST_Multi(geom),2236)));\nCREATE INDEX mdc_county_park_boundaries_geom_local_idx\n  ON mdc_county_park_boundaries\n  USING GIST (geom_local);\nNOTIFY pgrst, 'reload schema';\n",
    "processor": "GDSC automation (see Process Step)",
